 "_doc": "TRILINGUAL MASTHEAD LEDGER STATEMENT (MOSSEL BAY MUNICIPALITY / MOSSELBAAI MUNISIPALITEIT / UMASIPALA WASEMOSSELBAYI), 2 pages, always a real text layer (ocr never needed). FINGERPRINT: the municipality's OWN VAT number 4830118370 ('VAT No. / BTW Nr. 4830118370') plus the masthead string - 10/10 in this folder, 0/477 in the rest of the tree. The bill also prints 'VAT REG. NO. 4680101146', which is TELKOM's VAT (136 files across 17 folders here) - NEVER fingerprint on that. TEXT WRAPPER: page 1 and page 2 each begin with a print-stream mailer header like '<![number removed]||EMAIL|25|06|2024|1|3|1234|73543.00|1|F|E|nil|F|nil|nil|nil!>'. The account number inside that wrapper is NOT this account (it varies per page and per bill: [number removed], [number removed], [number removed]) - it is the mailer's own batch record. The account is read from 'ACCOUNT NUMBER:' in the bill body only. LAYOUT NOTE: the statement is set with rotated side-panel text (return address, contact details, payment notice), so PyMuPDF sort=True interleaves that text into the ledger lines. Every pattern is therefore written to tolerate arbitrary trailing junk on the line and never assumes a clean line end. SHAPES: page 1 is IDENTICAL on all 10 bills - ONE statement shape, no variants to handle. Page 2 has four variants and is the ONLY reason char count varies: (a) 5 bills (2026-02..2026-06) - page 2 holds nothing but the 106-char mailer wrapper; (b) 3 bills (2025-08, 2025-10, 2025-11) - 1,868 chars of stray rotated column captions (AMOUNT / VAT / TARIFF / VALUATION / DESCRIPTION) with no values; (c) 1 bill (2026-01) - 8,286 chars: the printed bilingual reverse side (Afrikaans/English terms of payment), total 20,457 chars, the biggest text in the folder; (d) 1 bill (2026-07) - 4,051 chars: a real RATES ADVICE block with rate-in-the-rand and financial year, the only bill where mos_rates_tariff_rate / mos_rates_year fill. File SIZE clusters (396KB x4 / 586KB x5 / 177KB x1) come from embedded artwork and are INVERSELY related to text volume - the 177KB file has the largest text (20.5k chars) and the 586KB files the smallest (12.1k) - so never infer shape from file size here. LEDGER SHAPE: '<dd/mm/yyyy> <code> <DESCRIPTION> [<period>]  <AMOUNT> *' where the trailing '*' means VAT applies and THE AMOUNT COLUMN IS VAT-INCLUSIVE. Electricity and water print their own 'VAT/BTW <amount>' sub-line, so ex-VAT for those is a genuine 'sub' compute. The statement foot prints \"VAT ON '*' ITEMS:\" = the total VAT on all starred lines. ELECTRICITY IS THREE LINES on one physical meter: [number removed] = kWh energy register (BASIC + energy rate line + VAT/BTW), [number removed]K = kVA maximum-demand register (rate line + VAT/BTW), and 'MIN MINIMUM' = the minimum-demand top-up. PROOF THAT MINIMUM IS AN ELECTRICITY CHARGE (it is unlabelled on the bill): MINIMUM ex-VAT / 488.513 (the printed kVA rate) + the billed kVA = exactly 100.0 kVA on every bill (18+82, 25+75, 26+74, ...), i.e. it tops the recorded demand up to a 100 kVA notified maximum demand. It is therefore mapped to nmd_r. CAVEAT, STATED PLAINLY: the MINIMUM line prints NO VAT of its own, so nmd_r carries the VAT-INCLUSIVE figure; ex-VAT is amount/1.15 (e.g. 41572.36 -> 36149.88) and the engine has no divide op. total_ex_vat_r is built the same way (inc-VAT amounts minus the printed VAT lines, MINIMUM at its printed inc-VAT value) so the reconcile is arithmetically consistent and NOT circular - MINIMUM cancels on both sides, and the check still genuinely tests the energy, basic and demand captures against the printed amount and VAT columns. nmd_kva (100) is NOT printed and is left blank. READINGS: '<prev> - <curr> (<units> <UNIT> <n> Days)' - PREVIOUS reading FIRST, current second, the OPPOSITE of Oudtshoorn's ledger. Not printed anywhere: reading type (Actual/Estimate), tariff name, TOU bands -> mapped '_none'. The '07/25' prefix on a rate line is the tariff EFFECTIVE month, not a tariff name. Money is plain dot-decimal with no thousands separator ('41572.36'); credits print a TRAILING minus ('95051.76-'), which the money cleaner handles. Dates are kept exactly as printed (dd/mm/yyyy). INDEPENDENT IDENTITY: \"VAT ON '*' ITEMS\" (printed) vs the derived per-line VAT (printed elec + kVA + water VAT lines, plus 15/115 of the unstarred-VAT lines MINIMUM/SEWERAGE/REFUSE) - max deviation R0.09 across the 10 bills (mean R0.06), all of it the bill's own per-line rounding of the 15/115 split. Second identity, exact to R0.00 on all 10: B/F BALANCE + RECEIPTS + every charge line + Balance Carried Forward = the printed AMOUNT DUE.",
